{"results":[{"record_id":"rec_000081","paper_type":"application_wrapper","generative_model_present":"no","foundation_model_evidence":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"application_wrapper","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"This is a web platform and reverse-pharmacology resource, not a new generative text-bio model. The abstract emphasizes curation, prediction tools, and APIs rather than a generative architecture.","evidence_snippet":"\"comprehensive web-based platform\"; \"Predict Target-SEA · Target2NP · MIDAS · NetVis · API\""},{"record_id":"rec_000082","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","generative_model_present":"no","foundation_model_evidence":"yes","primary_exclusion_code":"none","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"Unify is presented as a transfer-learning framework for universal cell embeddings, but the abstract does not describe a generative architecture. It does provide foundation-model-like evidence through use of protein language models and general-purpose language models for cross-species transfer.","evidence_snippet":"\"transfer learning framework\"; \"combining RNA expression with embeddings from protein language models and general-purpose language models\"; \"learns universal cell embeddings\""},{"record_id":"rec_000083","paper_type":"review_editorial","generative_model_present":"no","foundation_model_evidence":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"review_editorial","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"This is a review of plant single-cell and spatial multi-omics methods, not a primary model paper. It mentions foundation models only as a limitation of current plant data resources.","evidence_snippet":"\"This review summarizes experimental and computational approaches\"; \"limitations in applying foundation models to plant data\""},{"record_id":"rec_000084","paper_type":"review_editorial","generative_model_present":"yes","foundation_model_evidence":"unclear","primary_exclusion_code":"review_editorial","uncertainty_reaso